- Fix single-bottleneck-vector aggregation in dino/train_dino_transformer.py::DinoSelfAttention.forward_head
  (classifier head currently only reads x[:, 0, :], the CLS token):
  1. Concat CLS + mean-pooled frame tokens before the classifier head, i.e.
     cat([x[:, 0, :], x[:, 1:, :].mean(dim=1)]), double the head's input dim.
     Cheapest option, try first.
  2. Multiple aggregator tokens (replace single cls_token with N learnable query
     tokens, concat/pool their final states before the classifier head).
  Motivation: top-5-attention-frame check showed 11/17 grade-2-videos-misclassified-
  as-grade-0 had the frame-level DinoClassifier correctly predict grade 2 on at
  least one of those exact frames -> aggregator is losing signal that's present
  per-frame.

